From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 00:08:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/49] win32u: Clip foreign direct-draw children out of parent
 surfaces.

Some applications host CEF child windows that present directly from another
process. Under X11 the drawing process can fall back to using the toplevel
drawable, while the parent still owns an offscreen window surface. Full
parent surface flushes may then repaint stale backing-store contents over
the child, causing white or flickering client areas.

Add a dedicated SET_WINPOS_CLIP_CLIENT paint flag for windows whose client
area must be excluded from parent surfaces, and extend the existing pixel
format child clipping path to use it. Route the flag through an internal
message so foreign drawing processes can mark the owner window.

Mark X11 foreign direct draw child windows when GetDC() uses the toplevel
drawable, letting the parent surface clip out the child while the child
continues to present directly.

Fixes battle.net login window flickering / white window content under x11.
